<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/special_unitary.rs. No dependency beyond std. Exact integer arithmetic only. GaussianInteger{real,imaginary:i64}; GaussianMatrix=Vec<Vec<GaussianInteger>>; ExactFraction{numerator,denominator:i128} in lowest terms, positive denominator, new() returns None on zero denominator. Conventions in the module doc comment and they MUST NOT change: su(N) = skew-Hermitian traceless matrices; inner product <X,Y> = -(1/N) Re tr(XY); Killing K(X,Y)=tr_{su(N)}(ad X ad Y) as a REAL trace over su(N); Casimir C defined by K = -C <.,.>. special_unitary_basis(N): E_ij-E_ji, i(E_ij+E_ji) for i<j, and i*diag(1,..,1,-k,0,..) with k ones, k=1..N-1; orthogonal for -Re tr; None for N<2. killing_form(basis,X,Y)=sum_i B(e_i,[X,[Y,e_i]])/B(e_i,e_i), B=-Re tr; MUST NOT use the closed formula 2N tr(XY). special_unitary_casimir_constant(N) derives C from every basis pair and returns None if K is not proportional to the inner product. Independent tests: tests/special_unitary_casimir.rs (C=2N^2 for N=2..5, K=2N tr on all pairs for N=2..4, basis properties, negative control). Snake_case spelled-out names.
